23:03:02 said  GitHub is gone completely. Syncing now only runs between your local folder and a sync folder you choose in the settings, for example your Hugo blog. Each run reads only the new `transaction-JJJJ-MM-TT-HH-mm.json` files from the last processed timestamp on, imports new articles and overwrites existing ones, then writes your own changes plus a new transaction file. The "Vollsynchronisierung" button in the settings compares all articles in both folders. I tested this with two simulated computers, including several transaction files in the same minute, and it worked.
23:03:03 said  As you asked in between, the project is now called **hmb**, with a README that explains the name stands for Hugo Microblogger; your existing settings carry over. Still untested: the right-click entry under "Dienste" and the menu-bar icon.
