14:21:26 said  I built both epics, and the build and all 13 tests pass.
14:21:26 said  **Profiles:** On the main page there's now a dropdown at the top left. Each profile is one Hugo site with a title of up to 32 characters, its own data folder, its own sync folder and its own Git repository. Switching loads that site's articles and syncs against that site's sync folder. Your existing settings became the first profile, named "pearls" after your Hugo site.
14:21:26 said  **Git:** A new "Git" button sits next to Neu, Snippets and Synchronisieren. It opens a window with three steps:
14:21:26 said  - **Pull** gets new changes from the server and then offers "Jetzt synchronisieren".
14:21:26 said  - **Commit** lists what is new, changed or deleted since the last commit. The proposed message starts with the most recently changed entry and lists the three groups below it.
14:21:26 said  - **Push** sends the commits; Git's output, including the push message, appears at the bottom of the window.
14:21:26 said  I tested all three steps against a local test repository, not against your real server.
14:21:26 said  **Something that changes your blog on the next start:** I found and fixed a bug. Because your sync folder is `pearls/content/post`, hmb had been writing transactions, snippets and tags into `pearls/content/`, inside Hugo's content. On the next start, hmb moves these three items to `pearls/`, next to `content`. I tested this on a copy and the articles stayed untouched. You'll then see these moves in Git.
14:21:26 said  **Still open:**
14:21:26 said  - The app still warns about a duplicate folder: there are copies in `post/post` in both your blog and your app folder. "Doppelte Ordner reparieren" in the settings cleans them up.
14:21:28 said  - The guide with screenshots now lives outside the app folder, so I didn't change it. If you want, I can add pictures of the profiles and the Git window.
